  "prefLabel": "Cul-H 102.44 State curator",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cul-H 102.44 “State curator” means “state curator as defined in RSA 227-C:1, IX-a, namely “the member of the professional staff, designated by the director of the division of historical resources with the approval of the commissioner, charged with the identification, evaluation, protection, and interpretation of state owned objects of historic significance.”\n\nSource. #10217, eff 10-30-12, EXPIRED: 7-1-18",
